## Why This Is Asked

This question tests practical understanding of observability in a lightweight Azure stack, covering frontend-backend instrumentation, tracing continuity, log routing, and alerting, plus a minimal CI/CD workflow.

## Key Concepts

- Application Insights integration in SPA and Azure Functions
- End-to-end tracing with correlation IDs
- Log Analytics workspace and log routing
- Alerts for latency spikes and error rates
- Cost considerations for observability including sampling strategies
- CI/CD wiring with GitHub Actions for Azure Static Web Apps and Functions

## Code Example

```javascript
// SPA: generate correlation ID and pass in requests
const correlationId = crypto.randomUUID();

// Store in session for consistency
sessionStorage.setItem('correlationId', correlationId);

// Include in API requests
fetch('/api/data', {
  headers: {
    'x-correlation-id': correlationId
  }
});
```

```javascript
// Azure Function: read and log correlation ID
module.exports = async function (context, req) {
  const correlationId = req.headers['x-correlation-id'] || crypto.randomUUID();

  context.log.info('Processing request', { correlationId });

  context.res = {
    body: { data: [] },
    headers: { 'x-correlation-id': correlationId }
  };
};
```

## Cost Considerations

- **Application Insights**: Starts with 5 GB free per month; implement sampling (typically 10-30%) for high-traffic apps
- **Log Analytics**: Pay-per-GB ingestion; retention defaults to 30 days
- **Azure Static Web Apps**: Free tier available
- **Azure Functions**: Consumption plan with pay-per-execution pricing
- **Alerts**: First 10,000 alerts are free monthly

## Why This Is Asked
This question tests practical knowledge of observability in a beginner Azure stack, ensuring the candidate can wire instrumentation, telemetry exports, and basic dashboards end-to-end.

## Key Concepts
- OpenTelemetry integration in Azure Functions
- Application Insights exporter and per-endpoint metrics
- Sampling, traces, and dashboards in Azure Monitor
- GitHub Actions CI/CD for deployments
- Front Door TLS endpoint configuration
- SQL Auto Failover Group for cross-region DR

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal OpenTelemetry setup (Node.js)
const { NodeSDK } = require('@opentelemetry/sdk-node');
const { getNodeAutoInstrumentations } = require('@opentelemetry/auto-instrumentations-node');
const { AzureMonitorTraceExporter } = require('@opentelemetry/exporter-azure-monitor');

const sdk = new NodeSDK({
  traceExporter: new AzureMonitorTraceExporter({
    connectionString: process.env.APPLICATIONINSIGHTS_CONNECTION_STRING
  }),
  instrumentations: [getNodeAutoInstrumentations()],
  sampler: new AlwaysParentSampler(0.2) // 20% sampling
});

sdk.start();
```

